PATH RECONCILIATION (binding, honest)
  The generated prompt's templated Output/Allowed path
  `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/**` is NOT the compiled canonical home.
  project.yml compiles `Sources/`, and every shipped P7 *page* lives under
  `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Category>/` (ActiveSessions, ApiPlayground, AuditLog…).
  The page is therefore implemented at the REAL, compiled convention:
  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/**. Navigation registration
  (AppRoute/AppRouteParser/TeslaSyncApp) + the string catalog are the prompt's
  other allowed surfaces. (Same reconciliation as the sibling ActiveSessions log.)

SCOPE (honesty covenant: no scope-narrowing #2, no stubs as final #4, ADR-011)
  The web source HelixPage.tsx is page chrome (PageContainer: breadcrumb
  `Integrations / Helix`, title + subtitle) wrapping <AISettings/>. The thin page
  manifest record lists only the 2-3 page strings + the loading/success states, but
  a title-only screen would be a stub. AISettings is NOT a separate parity unit, so
  its FULL functional surface is reproduced natively (no narrowing):
    • Master mode radiogroup off / local-only / cloud (+ off banner)  [ADR-015 default-off]
    • Provider configuration: provider picker, model, local base-URL + Validate(+banner)
      + local explainer; Azure surface/API-version/chat-deployment/embedding-deployment +
      resource endpoint URL; cloud API key (secure) + daily cost cap + Validate(+banner)
    • Restore-previous-selection prompt (archived feature preview + Restore / No thanks)
      [ADR-015 §I7 — never silent]
    • Per-feature opt-in list — ALL 57 features, generated from a native port of the web
      AI registry (web `@/ai/features`, itself generated from internal/ai/features/registry.go)
    • Usage-today card (tokens in / out / estimated cost, em-dash fallbacks)
    • Cloud cost-cap spend bar (warn ≥80%, critical ≥100%, matching the backend BannerLevel)
    • Save flow (off omits provider/cap so the redact+archive path runs; key never leaks)
    • Data states loading / loaded(success) / error(retry)

