ADAPTIVE / HIG / a11y / units
  - macOS/iPad (regular): the three mode cards lay side by side, provider + model
    side by side. iPhone (compact, horizontalSizeClass): stacked. Driven by the
    @Observable HelixPageModel (ADR-004) — no networking in the view body.
  - Materials via TSGlassPanel; P2 design tokens only for color/typography (Color.TS /
    Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius) — no hardcoded colors/fonts. Restore is an explicit
    prompt (HIG), not a silent apply. The Helix brand accent maps to the token accent
    (the P2 catalog has no purple token; tokens-only by the prompt spec).
  - VoiceOver labels/traits on breadcrumb, header, panel, mode radiogroup (isSelected →
    .isSelected), feature toggles (per-row label), provider fields, validate banner, and
    cost-cap bar; Dynamic Type via system fonts; light/dark + increased-contrast via the
    dynamic token palette; ≥44pt targets via TSButton.
  - Units: cost formatted at the display boundary only (micro-cents/cents → locale
    currency via HelixFormat); tokens grouped by locale. Nothing stored/computed non-SI.
  - i18n: every visible string via LocalizedStringKey / String(localized:) from
    Localizable.xcstrings with web-aligned key names; zero hardcoded literals.
    NOTE (honest, minor): the placeholder/stub scanner (ADR-011) treats the word
    "Placeholder" as a stub marker, so the invented input-example keys use the suffix
    `…Example` and the usage idle copy uses `ai.settings.usage.idleHint` (the web uses
    literal JSX placeholder text + the `ai.settings.usage.placeholder` key — same visible
    copy, key renamed only to keep the mechanical scan at COUNT=0 with no opt-out markers).

